{#- explanation #}

<details><summary><b>Explanation</b></summary>

**Quality gates** are bounds checks on `quality_gate_*` experiments. A gate fails if any replicate of the comparison variant falls outside its configured bound; a single failed replicate fails the gate. These are what the CI job's pass/fail is based on.

**Optimization goals** are A/B comparisons of the comparison variant against the baseline. A change is flagged as a regression when |Δ mean %| ≥ **{{ effect_size | fmt2 }}%** in the regressing direction for the experiment's goal AND its **{{ confidence | fmt2 }}%** confidence interval excludes zero. Reduction in CPU or memory is an improvement; reduction in throughput is a regression. The Δ mean % cell is coloured accordingly: 🟢 improvement, 🔴 regression, ⚪ neutral. Optimization-goal changes are reported but do not fail this job.

Ping [#single-machine-performance](https://dd.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03LY8MQ73R) for help interpreting a report.

</details>
